  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As it is currently, the localization strings do not have glossary entries for VRChat concepts like \"Visitor\".\n\nThis will make it so that translations containing these words will confusingly use different vocabulary in each sentence that uses them. It is not particularly helpful for other language users if the UI shows one word for \"Visitor\", and the tooltips/explanation show another word, despite them being the same in English.\n\nIndeed, I can already see this happening in the Japanese translation, and it probably is happening in the other languages as well.\n\nWhen I used to do translations for Discord (back when they still used Crowdin), they used the 'Glossary' function to mark concepts. This makes the definition of the concept, and optionally a chosen equivalent per language, come up wherever the word appears in the localization files.\n\nVRChat's project should be using this feature to ensure the vocabulary is consistent, else if it is too confusing I feel as though people will just discourage the use of translations (given they have figured it out up to now anyway).",
